---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="How a CS start turned into Computer Engineering, and why the hardware–software seam is the interesting place to work."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        I started at Purdue in Computer Science, moved into First-Year Engineering for the
        hardware exposure, and landed in Computer Engineering, where the interesting problems
        turned out to be. What I like is the seam: the point where an algorithm has to become
        fixed-point arithmetic, become RTL, become a board that boots.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what I build lives on that seam. <a href="/projects/harmonicore/">HarmoniCore</a>
        is an audio effects processor in SystemVerilog, where every effect had to survive the
        trip from a Python reference model to fixed-point hardware that matches it within a
        couple of least significant bits. The
        <a href="/projects/socet-scoreboard/"> SoCET Scoreboard</a> is an FPGA design that also
        had to become a physical board, which is a completely different set of failure modes.
        <a href="/projects/stars-cdp/">STARS CDP</a> is RTL for a digital FM receiver heading
        toward silicon, and on
        <a href="/projects/psp-active-controls/"> Active Controls</a> I write firmware for an
        engine-controller interface board, which is the same instincts applied to a system where
        being wrong is expensive.
      </p>
      <p>
        I&#8217;m a sophomore graduating {SITE.gradDate}. Right now I&#8217;m most interested in
        FPGA and ASIC design, embedded software, and the systems side of AI infrastructure;
        roles where knowing both halves of the stack is the point rather than a curiosity.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="todo">TODO: one or two sentences that are actually yours. What drew you to
        the hardware side, or what you want to be doing in five years. This is the paragraph
        that stops the page reading like a résumé.</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside that: climbing, hiking, baking, and an unreasonable amount of thought about
        Commander deck construction, which is closer to constraint-solving than it sounds.
      </p>

      <h2>Reaching me</h2>
      <p>
        Email is best: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. I&#8217;m also on
        <a href={SITE.github}> GitHub</a> and <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
